census_records_one already establishes that a matching sha suppresses PV-ONT-020. So this test exercises only the missing-command path (PV-ONT-019) and never constructs the case that would also draw PV-ONT-020 (e.g. a mismatched or absent sha). The assertion itself is correct for its actual inputs; the function name overpromises what it demonstrates -- a reader trusting the name would believe the both-rules-at-once case is covered when it is not."},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"crates/aprender-contracts/src/lint/evidence_gate_tests.rs"},"region":{"startLine":143,"endLine":145}}}],"properties":{"grounding":"measured","command":["sed","-n","110,170p","crates/aprender-contracts/src/lint/evidence_gate_tests.rs"],"exit_code":0,"stdout_sha256":"64386ecdcd33b5f7272eedf6bf74f35fbe062edfda26774d0273bebe20075bc7","failure_scenario":"A future change to rules_with's PV-ONT-020 logic that silently stops firing when it should would pass this test unnoticed, because the test never constructs an input where PV-ONT-020 is expected to fire alongside PV-ONT-019 -- the name's claim of dual coverage is not backed by the assertion.","precision_class":"advisory"}}]},{"tool":{"driver":{"name":"nvidia-cuda-docs","version":"n/a","informationUri":"https://docs.nvidia.com/cuda/","rules":[]}},"invocations":[{"executionSuccessful":true,"toolExecutionNotifications":[{"level":"note","message":{"text":"CUDA_MSG_RE/path trigger fires on 2 of 563 changed paths at the corrected base_sha, both false-positive filename matches with no device-behavior claim: crates/aprender-contracts-cli/tests/fixtures/pvl/obligations/pmat/src/tdg/cuda_simd_scores.rs.txt (new test fixture; a data file of recorded TDG scores, matched on the literal substring 'cuda' in its path, not on device semantics) and crates/aprender-contracts-staging/lean/Challenge/fp8-interchange-v1.lean (new Lean proof file about the fp8 interchange numeric format, matched on 'fp8', which is a data-format term here, not a CUDA/PTX device-behavior claim)."},"properties":{"grounding":"measured","command":["bash","scripts/check_pr_review_receipt.sh","--match-path","<each of 563 changed paths>"],"exit_code":0,"stdout_sha256":null}},{"level":"note","message":{"text":"no-authority-found: queried whether either matched file makes any CUDA/PTX/device-behavior claim requiring NVIDIA doc authority. Neither does -- one is fixture data, one is a numeric-format proof with no GPU execution semantics."},"properties":{"grounding":"measured","command":["nvidia-cuda-docs","search","does the ONT-8 evidence-gate diff make a CUDA/GPU device-behavior claim"],"exit_code":0,"stdout_sha256":null}}]}],"results":[]},{"tool":{"driver":{"name":"crux","version":"n/a","informationUri":"internal","rules":[]}},"invocations":[{"executionSuccessful":true,"toolExecutionNotifications":[{"level":"note","message":{"text":"CRUX_SURFACE_RE fires 31 times in crates/aprender-contracts-cli/src/cli.rs across the corrected 563-file diff -- real clap derive(Parser)/derive(Subcommand)/long=/short= additions accumulated over the whole 7af7cc17b..fe0acafc7 branch history, not solely the ONT-8 evidence gate (which adds no new CLI surface of its own)."},"properties":{"grounding":"measured","command":["grep","-noE","CRUX_SURFACE_RE","crates/aprender-contracts-cli/src/cli.rs"],"exit_code":0,"stdout_sha256":null}}]}],"results":[{"ruleId":"crux/no-coverage-for-new-cli-surface","level":"note","message":{"text":"pv's internal CLI surface (crates/aprender-contracts-cli/src/cli.rs) has zero contracts/crux-*.yaml coverage: none of that directory's contract categories or competitor fields address the provable-contracts CLI itself. Coverage gap, not a regression -- there is no prior competitive claim this diff widens or closes."},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"crates/aprender-contracts-cli/src/cli.rs"}}}],"properties":{"grounding":"measured","command":["grep","-rl","provable-contracts CLI","contracts/crux-*.yaml"],"exit_code":1,"stdout_sha256":null,"failure_scenario":"A breaking change to pv's own CLI surface (a renamed flag, a removed subcommand) has no CRUX contract to catch it, so it would ship undetected by this gate.","precision_class":"advisory"}}]},{"tool":{"driver":{"name":"cargo-mutants","version":"n/a","informationUri":"https://mutants.rs/","rules":[]}},"invocations":[{"executionSuccessful":false,"toolExecutionNotifications":[{"level":"error","message":{"text":"MUTATION_TRIGGER_RE fires: 33 changed scripts/check_*.sh files plus a .github/workflows/ci.yml hunk in the 7af7cc17b..fe0acafc7 window are guard-touching. Grepped all 5 existing mutate-*.sh scripts (mutate-guard.sh, mutate_pr_review_wiring_guard.sh, mutate_quorum_arm.sh, mutate_spec_conformance.sh, mutate_vendored_schemas_guard.sh): none targets any of the 33 newly-changed scripts (only check_pr_review_receipt.sh, check_pr_review_counts.sh, check_pr_review_wiring.sh and check_vendored_schemas.sh are covered by any mutate-*.sh script, and none of those 4 is among the 33). No committed mutation-kill set exists for this diff's guard-touching surface -- consultation could not run to a killed/survivor count."},"properties":{"grounding":"measured","command":["grep","-l","check_","scripts/mutate-guard.sh","scripts/mutate_pr_review_wiring_guard.sh","scripts/mutate_quorum_arm.sh","scripts/mutate_spec_conformance.sh","scripts/mutate_vendored_schemas_guard.sh"],"exit_code":0,"stdout_sha256":null}}]}],"results":[{"ruleId":"mutation/no-committed-set-for-new-guards","level":"warning","message":{"text":"33 changed check_*.sh guard scripts + a ci.yml hunk ship with no committed mutation-kill set (same structural cause as the prior 7af7cc17b receipt's own DEGRADED, for a different/overlapping file set). A defect in any of their bash conditionals would not be caught by any of this repo's 5 existing mutate-*.sh scripts."},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":".github/workflows/ci.yml"}}}],"properties"